{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785183896,"nonce":"m4FN2AzfRHi4yio+pfsA9mmtky8=","title":"ADR-0062 s9 (HITL): measure operations-per-second under latency for a cargo-shaped write load","message":"**The one unpriced number in ADR-0062**, and the number that decides whether s7 is an accelerator or a requirement.\n\nMeasure a `cargo build`-shaped workload against a real in-cluster Export. **Byte throughput is not the thing to measure** — NFS charges a round-trip per file operation, and a build that creates, writes and `fsync`s many small files pays latency per file that no bandwidth fixes. Measure ops/sec under latency, plus the Farm build time for 50k files.\n\nHITL because the result is a decision, not a diff.\n\n\n- [ ] Reports ops/sec and per-operation latency for create/write/fsync/stat/unlink at realistic file counts, not aggregate MB/s\n- [ ] Reports Farm build time for a ~50k-file tree, and **states which rung ran** (reflink vs copy)\n- [ ] **Fails loudly if it silently falls back a rung** — a spike that reports a flattering number because reflink or `overlayfs` was unavailable is the exact failure this repo has already paid for\n- [ ] Compares against the measured status quo (ADR-0061 s0/s2 tables) on the same machine shape\n- [ ] Written up in ADR-0062's Open section, replacing the placeholder\n- [ ] A `just` recipe, so the next person can re-run it\n\n\n- s5 (needs a real Export to measure)","files":null}]}